 "pdf": "ads5553.pdf",
 "pages": "p.2 (ROC: AVDD/DRVDD 3.0-3.6 V), p.6 (timing: tSTART 4.5 ns max, latency 16.5 clocks), p.7-8 (pins), p.19 (Table 2 PDN/OEA/OEB), p.21 (output information: two's complement, OVR, CLKOUT, OE)",
 "notModeled": [
  "channel B is not modeled: the clocked bus carries one clock and at most 24 data pins, so only channel A (CLKPA, OVRA + D13A..D0A, OEA, CLKOUTA) is driven; D13B..D0B, OVRB and CLKOUTB are never driven, OEB/CLKPB/CLKMB are ignored",
  "analog input, internal/external reference (REFSEL), IREF and CM biasing; the result is always the 0 V code 0 (two's complement)",
  "pipeline latency 16.5 clock cycles not modeled (the code is constant); data valid tSTART (4.5 ns max at 65 MSPS) after the input clock; CLKOUTA shares tOut",
  "OVRA (over-range) is driven as the top data bit, always 0 at 0 V",
  "CLKPA/CLKMA are a differential (or single-ended) sampling clock: the model clocks on CLKPA alone",
  "PDN (Table 2): PDN high powers down the ADC channels whose OE is low; with OEA high channel A stays on, and with OEA low its outputs are already high-impedance, so PDN has no visible effect on the modeled channel and is not modeled; power-down by a clock below 10 MSPS not modeled",
  "OE to stable output timing (1000 clock cycles) not modeled",
  "vcc is the DRVDD range; the pin table lists DRVDD as 4 pins but gives 5 numbers (34, 42, 49, 57, 65); all five are DRVDD here"
